WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:00.850
Good morning, Hank, it's Wednesday.

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:02.290
Great top ten list on Monday;

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:07.090
today, it's time for my top ten list:
Top Ten Animal Power Moves!

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.675
...God, I love power moves.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.060
Power move number ten belongs to the Bombardier beetle.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.960
Hank, when the Bombardier beetle is threatened,

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:17.779
it turns around and sprays boiling hot acid
out of its butt!

00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:19.220
Power move number nine: giraffes.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.460
You know how I love giraffes, Hank.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:22.859
Giraffes are like the Chuck Norris of the
animal kingdom.

00:00:22.959 --> 00:00:25.370
When they roundhouse kick you, 
you forget what time it is.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.649
A giraffe kick has been known to 
decapitate a lion!

00:00:28.749 --> 00:00:31.330
Power move number eight, and one of my personal favorites,

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.730
comes from Cantor's giant softshell turtle.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.629
Now, Hank, we know 
the power move for regular turtles:

00:00:35.729 --> 00:00:36.859
it's their hard green shells,

00:00:36.959 --> 00:00:38.685
and we know the power move for red turtles:

00:00:38.785 --> 00:00:40.610
it's their heat-seeking red shells.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:44.410
But the power move for a softshell turtle
is motionlessness.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:46.829
Yes, Hank, Cantor's softshell turtle covers
himself with sand

00:00:46.929 --> 00:00:49.520
 in a riverbank
and then sits completely still

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:54.589
for twenty-three and a half hours a day,
moving only when something crosses his path

00:00:54.689 --> 00:00:55.479
that he can eat.

00:00:55.579 --> 00:00:56.869
That actually sounds a lot like my life,

00:00:56.969 --> 00:00:59.209
only Cantor's softshell turtle gets to live
on the beach

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:00.799
and I have to live in Indianapolis.

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:03.889
Power move number seven belongs to Trichobatrachus Robostus,

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:05.459
which is a frog, and when he's threatened

00:01:05.559 --> 00:01:09.560
he breaks a bone in his own foot
and then uses the bone fragment

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:13.340
from his compound fracture
as a claw to stab you!

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.680
Power move number six is the cuttlefish.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.120
So, Hank, cuttlefish can turn into crazy colours.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.570
They can light up blue and green 
and orange and yellow,

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:24.550
and they'll swim over to some prey,
and they'll start lighting up, as if to say,

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:28.389
"Here's the party! Check it out!
I'm a disco ball! Come and party with me!

00:01:28.489 --> 00:01:29.479
This is a crazy rave!

00:01:29.579 --> 00:01:30.069
OH WAIT!

00:01:30.169 --> 00:01:31.229
You just got eaten."

00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:33.589
Power move number five: baby potato beetles.

00:01:33.689 --> 00:01:35.649
Hank, grown-up potato beetles have hard shells,

00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:37.509
which makes it harder for predators to eat them,

00:01:37.609 --> 00:01:39.920
but baby potato beetles don't.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.670
Fortunately, they have poisonous poop.

00:01:42.770 --> 00:01:46.920
It's so rare in life that the word 'fortunately'
precedes the words 'they have poisonous poop.'

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:49.320
So what the baby potato beetles do is

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.079
they poop and then they cover 
their whole bodies

00:01:52.179 --> 00:01:54.300
in that poisonous poop to discourage predators.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:55.720
Power move!

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.310
Power move number four: Mabra elephantophila.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:00.300
Hank, we all know that 
elephants have awesome power moves

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.540
like stomping and painting pictures,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.345
but I would argue that the moth Mabra elephantophila

00:02:05.445 --> 00:02:07.750
has an even better power move,

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.755
which is feasting on the tears of elephants.

00:02:09.855 --> 00:02:11.460
Yes, Hank, there is a moth that gets most

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.080
of its sustenance from eating elephant tears,

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:15.050
and when the elephants aren't crying
enough on their own,

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:18.930
the moth will go in and scratch at their eyes to make them cry more.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.820
Power move number three: 
the Australian funnel-web spider.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.640
Hank, everybody in America is so afraid of
Black Widow spiders,

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:29.360
but funnel-web spiders in Australia are like
for real with their power moves.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:35.450
For instance, they're very aggressive, and
their fangs can shoot through human fingernails.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.525
[Cell phone rings]

00:02:37.625 --> 00:02:39.800
...That's so scary, someone had to 
call me about it.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.900
Power move number two: the duck billed platypus.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:45.760
Hank, not only are platypi one of the very
few mammals that lay eggs,

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:50.650
they also have a sixth sense - no joke -
called 'electrolocation.'

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.160
Platypi can use their fat little bills to
sense electromagnetic fields,

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:58.120
which means that the moment one of their predators moves a muscle -

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.730
literally contracts a muscle -

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:03.140
the platypi knows which direction 
that muscle is headed.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.400
It's like a literal superpower,

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.860
only it's contained 
inside of a glorified beaver.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.585
And Hank, my number-one power move in the
animal kingdom goes to

00:03:09.685 --> 00:03:12.083
camponotus saundersi, a carpenter ant.

00:03:12.183 --> 00:03:13.780
So, Hank, when this ant is in a fight and

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:17.410
he notices that he's going to lose,
instead of like fighting to the death or whatever,

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:21.530
he gets as close to his prey as possible,
and then blows himself up.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.680
These ants have these poisonous glands that
run the entire length of their body,

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.880
and when they realize 
they're about to lose a fight,

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:31.560
they contract their abdominal muscles so intensely
that their entire body explodes,

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.405
sending the poison flying.

00:03:33.505 --> 00:03:34.650
Nerdfighters, I can't wait to read

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:36.640
your favorite animal power moves in the comments.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.530
It's been fascinating to read about all of the diseases that you have.

00:03:39.630 --> 00:03:42.110
Hank, I will see you and 
your last top ten list on Friday;

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:46.410
don't forget to be awesome.

